{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bb003f551257c34a","name":"KDY-4 Tech Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-bb003f551257c34a","title":"KDY-4 Tech Droid","revision":20890,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:43:36Z","sha256":"6f316f2eebcf84139482a55c24a36416dd10870274362a5fc03907270d107ed6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20890","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=KDY-4%20Tech%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bb003f551257c34a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The KDY-4 Tech Droid is loved by mechanics, shipbuilders, and grease monkeys of all types. Designed by Kuat Drive Yards, the KDY-4 is commonly called the builder's buddy because of its utilitarian design, efficiency, and easygoing manner. KDY-4s are found at nearly every shipyard, and larger vessels keep some on board to repair heavy damage that exceeds the abilities of Astromechs.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The KDY-4 boasts four ",{"tag":"a","children":["Appendages"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Appendages"},", two of which can be retracted out of the way of delicate repairs. Its three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Magnetic Feet"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Magnetic_Feet","referenceId":"reference:16c326e31f21c93f"}," give it unparalleled stability as it clambers on hulls or makes its way through the twisted metal of damaged interiors. Its servomotors are augmented to give it the equivalent lifting power of a strong humanoid, which is useful for hauling heavy equipment or securing durasteel in place for welding.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The memory banks of these Droids contain the blueprints of every ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," commonly available in a given era. Owners augment this massive database with more ship designs as they obtain them. This augmentation creates an unintended side effect, however, because most owners are reluctant to perform routine ",{"tag":"a","children":["Memory Wipes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Memory_Wipes"}," on their KDY-4s for fear of corrupting or losing this valuable and expensive data. Thus, KDY-4s develop the personality quirks common among other ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droids","referenceId":"reference:a314fe9a0993afad"},", such as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["R2-Series Astromech Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/R2-Series_Astromech_Droid","referenceId":"reference:fec1452b3294defc"},", but KDY-4s have a propensity for more upbeat, even chirpy mannerisms.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["KDY-4 Tech Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["KDY-4 Tech Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 2 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag